      <activity id="0a8e2392-e984-5c57-b5b1-d9e9eedf627b" activityNameId="04a1bb62-0a6f-5217-a417-b1c4ca0793b5" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Heat, at 10.5 m2 evacuated tube collector, heat pipe, one-family house, for combined system</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Heat, at 10.5 m2 evacuated tube collector, heat pipe, one-family house, for combined system
Use of a solar system with heat pipes excluding the necessary auxiliary heating. The simulation is made for solar collector systems in the city of Zurich. The annual irradiation amounts to 1249 kWh/m2. 33% solar fraction, 35° inclination, 22° southeast orientation.;
UUID: b5324f06-bba0-3542-a1e8-754db2d0a0f4
Delivery of heat with a solar system including maintenance and electricity use for operation. Excluding the necessary auxiliary heating.
Location: Solar collector system operated in CH.
Technology: Solar collector system for hot water installed on the roof of a house.
Time period: Time of simulation.
Production volume: Total solar heat delivered by evacuated tube collectors in 2001 was 2.3TJ.
Sampling: Own simulation. 
Extrapolations: none
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_b5324f06-bba0-3542-a1e8-754db2d0a0f4.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
